{"@context":{"tg":"https://example.org/threatgraph/vocab#","dcterms":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/","dcat":"http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#","prov":"http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#","rdfs":"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#","xsd":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#","Vulnerability":"tg:Vulnerability","NvdRecord":"tg:NvdRecord","CvssV31":"tg:CvssV31","Weakness":"tg:Weakness","WeaknessAssignment":"tg:WeaknessAssignment","AttackTechnique":"tg:AttackTechnique","AttackTactic":"tg:AttackTactic","Mapping":"tg:Mapping","Dataset":"dcat:Dataset","Distribution":"dcat:Distribution","apiUrl":{"@id":"tg:apiUrl","@type":"@id"},"wasDerivedFrom":{"@id":"prov:wasDerivedFrom","@type":"@id","@container":"@set"},"name":"rdfs:label","description":"dcterms:description","title":"dcterms:title","cveId":"dcterms:identifier","vendorProject":"tg:vendorProject","product":"tg:product","shortDescription":"tg:shortDescription","requiredAction":"tg:requiredAction","dateAdded":{"@id":"tg:dateAdded","@type":"xsd:date"},"dueDate":{"@id":"tg:dueDate","@type":"xsd:date"},"ransomwareUse":"tg:ransomwareUse","notes":"tg:notes","dueBeforeAdded":"tg:dueBeforeAdded","weakness":{"@id":"tg:weakness","@container":"@set"},"nvd":"tg:nvdRecord","mappings":{"@id":"tg:hasMapping","@container":"@set"},"cweId":"tg:cweId","isInformative":"tg:isInformative","vulnStatus":"tg:vulnStatus","published":{"@id":"dcterms:issued","@type":"xsd:dateTime"},"nReferences":"tg:nReferences","cvssV31":"tg:cvssV31","cvssV2Score":{"@id":"tg:cvssV2Score","@type":"xsd:decimal"},"score":{"@id":"tg:baseScore","@type":"xsd:decimal"},"severity":"tg:severity","vector":"tg:vector","metricSource":"tg:metricSource","metricType":"tg:metricType","weaknessAssignment":{"@id":"tg:weaknessAssignment","@container":"@set"},"assignedBy":"tg:assignedBy","assignmentType":"tg:assignmentType","techniqueId":"tg:techniqueId","tacticId":"tg:tacticId","shortname":"tg:shortname","status":"tg:status","isSubtechnique":"tg:isSubtechnique","created":{"@id":"dcterms:created","@type":"xsd:dateTime"},"modified":{"@id":"dcterms:modified","@type":"xsd:dateTime"},"parentTechnique":{"@id":"tg:parentTechnique","@type":"@id"},"subtechnique":{"@id":"tg:subtechnique","@type":"@id","@container":"@set"},"tactic":{"@id":"tg:tactic","@container":"@set"},"technique":"tg:technique","vulnerability":"tg:vulnerability","mappingType":"tg:mappingType","capabilityGroup":"tg:capabilityGroup","comments":"tg:comments","evidence":{"@id":"tg:evidence","@container":"@set"},"evidenceUrl":{"@id":"tg:evidenceUrl","@type":"@id","@container":"@set"},"version":"dcterms:hasVersion","publisher":"dcterms:publisher","rights":"dcterms:rights","sha256":"tg:sha256","rawManifestSha256":"tg:rawManifestSha256","cleaningCodeSha256":"tg:cleaningCodeSha256","rowCount":"tg:rowCount","distribution":{"@id":"dcat:distribution","@container":"@set"},"accessURL":{"@id":"dcat:accessURL","@type":"@id"},"mediaType":{"@id":"dcat:mediaType","@container":"@set"},"tables":"tg:tables","totalItems":"tg:totalItems","nextPage":{"@id":"tg:nextPage","@type":"@id"},"previousPage":{"@id":"tg:previousPage","@type":"@id"}},"@id":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/","@type":"AttackTechnique","techniqueId":"T1190","apiUrl":"http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/techniques/T1190/","name":"Exploit Public-Facing Application","status":"active","isSubtechnique":false,"created":"2018-04-18T17:59:24.739000Z","modified":"2024-09-24T14:33:53.433000Z","description":"Adversaries may attempt to exploit a weakness in an Internet-facing host or system to initially access a network. The weakness in the system can be a software bug, a temporary glitch, or a misconfiguration.\n\nExploited applications are often websites/web servers, but can also include databases (like SQL), standard services (like SMB or SSH), network device administration and management protocols (like SNMP and Smart Install), and any other system with Internet-accessible open sockets.(Citation: NVD CVE-2016-6662)(Citation: CIS Multiple SMB Vulnerabilities)(Citation: US-CERT TA18-106A Network Infrastructure Devices 2018)(Citation: Cisco Blog Legacy Device Attacks)(Citation: NVD CVE-2014-7169) Depending on the flaw being exploited this may also involve [Exploitation for Defense Evasion](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1211) or [Exploitation for Client Execution](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1203).\n\nIf an application is hosted on cloud-based infrastructure and/or is containerized, then exploiting it may lead to compromise of the underlying instance or container. This can allow an adversary a path to access the cloud or container APIs (e.g., via the [Cloud Instance Metadata API](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/005)), exploit container host access via [Escape to Host](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1611), or take advantage of weak identity and access management policies.\n\nAdversaries may also exploit edge network infrastructure and related appliances, specifically targeting devices that do not support robust host-based defenses.(Citation: Mandiant Fortinet Zero Day)(Citation: Wired Russia Cyberwar)\n\nFor websites and databases, the OWASP top 10 and CWE top 25 highlight the most common web-based vulnerabilities.(Citation: OWASP Top 10)(Citation: CWE top 25)","tactic":[{"@id":"https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0001/","@type":"AttackTactic","tacticId":"TA0001","shortname":"initial-access","name":"Initial Access"}],"mappings":[{"@id":"urn:threatgraph:pkev-mapping:1","@type":"Mapping","mappingType":"exploitation_technique","wasDerivedFrom":["https://github.com/center-for-threat-informed-defense/mappings-explorer/tree/ddc842aa48c871cbfc2219cdbb842e9a4e155afe"],"technique":{"@id":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/","@type":"AttackTechnique","techniqueId":"T1190","name":"Exploit Public-Facing Application"},"vulnerability":{"@id":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-34102","@type":"Vulnerability","cveId":"CVE-2024-34102"}},{"@id":"urn:threatgraph:pkev-mapping:23","@type":"Mapping","mapping